# BMW 3 Series E46 four-door saloon, 1998-2005.
#
# The fourth 3-series: the rounded, wider body that replaced the E36, sold as
# saloon, coupe, convertible, Touring and Compact. The four-door saloon is
# modelled, the volume UK body.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_3_Series_(E46)
#
# Dimensions 4.470 x 1.735 x 1.415 m, wheelbase 2.725 m, for the saloon, from
# the English Wikipedia dimension box (wheelbase 2,725 mm; the box gives length,
# width and height per body style). Mirrors and rubbing strips take the modelled
# width past the body figure.
#
# Colours. No BMW UK colour card for the E46 was located; the four names come
# from an aftermarket paint-code list of 2003 3-series colours, which establishes
# the names as BMW finishes but not UK ordering:
#   Alpinweiss III          300, listed for 2003
#   Jet Black               668, listed for 2003
#   Titansilber metallic    354, listed for 2003
#   Orientblau metallic     317, listed for 2003
# UK availability is not established and the header says so; the M3-only
# colours (Laguna Seca Blue, Phoenix Yellow, Interlagos Blue) are deliberately
# excluded from a four-door saloon palette.
# Weights silver 3, black 3, white 2, blue 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 220 km/h for the volume 320i/325i; the 330i's 250 km/h limiter and the
# M3 are not modelled. Comfort 120/510, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 120, between the
# E36's 115/503 and the E90's 125/518. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: March 1998 intro, retires staggered
# 2014-2017 on a sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e46.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e46.dae (47 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e46/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the roof and
# rear quarter-glass outline are more angular than the photographs, the bumper
# ends are squared rather than rounded, and the wheel arches cut higher into the
# flank than the reference car, which makes the wheels read large at sprite
# scale. The builder flagged these itself and did not certify Gate B. At 128 px
# the car still reads as an E46-shape saloon, so no correction round was spent.

obj=citycar
name=BMW3E46(Titansilber)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1998
intro_month=3
retire_year=2017
retire_month=6
speed=220
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=120
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=510

